VERDICT
==================================================================================================================
  MY HYPOTHESIS IS REFUTED AND THE BLOCK GETS WORSE.  The run was launched on the idea that the pressure-supported
  block -- 20 of the 28 rows of the liability table -- is one wrong prescription, because the programme substituted nu
  into a Newtonian mass estimator instead of solving a Jeans equation.  It is not.  For a Plummer sphere the two agree
  to 0.8 per cent at every mass from 1e5 to 1e9 Msun, and the Jeans machinery -- validated against the Newtonian and
  deep-MOND limits by its own mutations -- buys nothing.
  What DOES matter is the external field, and it moves the block AGAINST the framework.  Decomposed: including the
  internal field in nu's argument is the dominant term, the sphere-averaged coupling from f01 contributes the ~0.04 dex
  it predicted, and the Jeans integration contributes almost nothing.  The Local Group dwarf offset grows.
  NET: the pressure-supported block is real, it was being UNDER-stated, and both corrections owed to it push the wrong
  way for the framework.  This is the opposite of what the run was launched to find.

